{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And this is the offering</b> — by way of truth, it is like \"And YHWH gave Solomon wisdom\" (I Kings 5:26), and thus it is written, \"And this is what their father spoke to them and blessed them\" (Genesis 49:28), and it is written, \"And this is the blessing\" (Deuteronomy 33:1), and it is written, \"From YHWH was this\" (Psalms 118:23). They already alluded to this in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 100:12) in the midrash on \"from the elders I will gain understanding\" (Psalms 119:100), and the discerning one will understand. And in Shemot Rabbah (49:2): \"And this is the offering that you shall take from them\" — this is the Congregation of Israel, which is the offering, as it is said, \"Israel is holy to YHWH, the first of His produce\" (Jeremiah 2:3). And there (Exodus Rabbah 33:1) He further said to them: The Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel: I sold you My Torah, and as it were, I was sold with it, as it is said, \"And they shall take for Me an offering\" (Exodus 25:2) — for the offering shall be for Me, and I am with it, in the manner of \"My beloved is mine and I am his\" (Song of Songs 2:16). And thus He said, \"according to all that I show you\" (Exodus 25:9), for I am He who shows, and He said, \"showing you\" (Exodus 27:8), a hint to the word \"I,\" and likewise \"that you show\" (Exodus 28:40). And thus David said, \"All is in writing from the hand of YHWH, He gave me understanding\" (I Chronicles 28:19), for the hand of YHWH was upon him."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase 'במדרש מזקנים אתבונן' likely refers to a homiletic reading of Psalms 119:100 where 'מזקנים' is read as 'from the elders,' i.e., from earlier sages; the exact attribution to Bereshit Rabbah 100:12 is preserved as Ramban cites it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:16:03.240385297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}